{"data": {"acceptance": ["kind 'whitespace' decision items render their exact source slice instead of an empty string in _render_document and _render_validated_window", "rendered cleaned text collapses runs of three or more newlines to exactly two so artifact removal adjacent to restored gaps cannot emit blank-line pileups", "two story blocks separated by a blank line in source render with the blank line intact instead of concatenated", "gates pass: uv run --directory 04_Software/AudioMancer pytest -q and uv run --directory 04_Software/AudioMancer ruff check ."], "assumptions": [], "created_at": "2026-07-26T21:33:11+00:00", "decision": "proceed", "open_questions": [], "planned_paths": [], "reason": "Classified low, not medium: the change is a few lines inside one pure rendering function with full deterministic test coverage, no persisted-format or schema change, nothing is committed, and the only real hazard - stale cleanup artifacts in existing projects - was explicitly waived by the user in chat. Human approval for this exact work was already given.", "recommended_responses": [], "risk": "low", "scope": ["04_Software/AudioMancer/src/audiomancer/services/ai_cleanup_service.py, 04_Software/AudioMancer/tests/test_ai_cleanup_contract.py, .agentic/requirements/functional/, .agentic/knowledge/components/"], "source": "Chat 2026-07-27: user reported translated text keeping PDF line wraps; analysis traced two independent defects in AI Cleanup. User approved implementing defect 1 then defect 2 independently on master, no commits, and stated backward compatibility is not a concern.", "understanding": "AI Cleanup classifies whitespace-only source gaps between returned blocks as restored_whitespace_ranges and persists them as decision items with kind 'whitespace', but both re-render paths (_render_document and _render_validated_window) emit an empty string for that kind, so the gap text is deleted. Paragraph breaks between two adjacent story blocks vanish, producing run-on text such as 'they were.Birch was once'. The text_cleanup_system prompt explicitly promises these gaps are restored from validated source positions."}, "event": "alignment.recorded", "time": "2026-07-26T21:33:11+00:00"}
